Relevant columns and their potential use
• “event_begin_time”: extract year & month to decide “past 15 years” range and to identify the “most‑affected month”.  
• “damage_property”: rank events, keep the top 100 with the greatest property loss.  
• “event_id”: treat every row as a unique severe‑storm event; handy when counting.  
• (any other columns are optional for the task, so not referenced in the core logic)

Typical conditions that may be used  
• Table filter → only yearly tables 2010‑2024 (15 years, inclusive).  
• Top‑100 filter → QUALIFY ROW_NUMBER() OVER (ORDER BY "damage_property" DESC)=… or LIMIT 100 after an ORDER BY.  
• Month filter → TO_TIMESTAMP("event_begin_time"/1e6) to turn micro‑second epoch into a timestamp, then DATE_TRUNC('month', …) or EXTRACT(month …).  

